,"start":-230,"end":300,"summary":"Mixed Germanic people of the lower Danube and Moldavia. Defeated by Marcus Licinius Crassus in 29-28 BC, when he killed their king Deldo with his own hand.","color":"#455C40"},{"id":"batavi","name":"Batavi","type":"tribe","family":"germanic","start":-50,"end":400,"summary":"Offshoot of the Chatti settled in the Rhine delta. Exempt from tribute in return for supplying soldiers, including the emperors' German bodyguard and eight auxiliary cohorts. Revolted under Julius Civilis in 69-70.","color":"#5F8862"},{"id":"belgae","name":"Belgic tribes","type":"confederation","family":"gallic","start":-300,"end":-51,"color":"#88B458"},{"id":"bithynia","name":"Kingdom of Bithynia","type":"kingdom","family":"anatolian","start":-297,"end":-74,"color":"#5B808A"},{"id":"blemmyes","name":"Blemmyes","type":"tribe","family":"other","start":250,"end":641,"color":"#93887C"},{"id":"boii","name":"Boii","type":"tribe","family":"gallic","start":-400,"end":-191,"color":"#88B457"},{"id":"bosporan_kingdom","name":"Bosporan Kingdom","type":"client_kingdom","family":"greek","start":-438,"end":370,"color":"#31718D"},{"id":"brigantes","name":"Brigantes","type":"client_kingdom","family":"british","start":-50,"end":71,"color":"#60896A"},{"id":"britons","name":"British tribes","type":"confederation","family":"british","start":-600,"end":43,"color":"#82A793"},{"id":"britons_sub_roman","name":"Sub-Roman Britons","type":"kingdom","family":"british","start":410,"end":641,"color":"#719C81"},{"id":"bructeri","name":"Bructeri","type":"tribe","family":"germanic","start":-100,"end":400,"summary":"Germanic people on the upper Ems and Lippe. Took part in the Varian disaster; Lucius Stertinius recovered the eagle of legio XIX from them in AD 15. Their seeress Veleda backed Civilis in 69-70.","color":"#618B65"},{"id":"bruttii","name":"Bruttii","type":"confederation","family":"italic","start":-356,"end":-272,"color":"#AB8E4B"},{"id":"bulgars","name":"Bulgars","type":"nomadic","fam